Design notes: the flag package calls FlagSet.Usage both for -h/--help and before every parse failure, and ContinueOnError also prints the error to Output — so each FlagSet gets io.Discard output and a Usage that renders into a per-command buffer; the caller flushes the buffer to stdout only on flag.ErrHelp. cliMain(args,stdout,stderr) int is the testable exit-code mapping behind the 3-line main; process-level tests fork through TestMain's child-run role. Bare dispatch levels (ohya, ohya devices) print help and exit 0, mirroring --help. Post-parse validation errors (missing/extra positional args, non-positive --interval/--ttl, wildcard listen without --control-url) are usage errors: exit 2.
